      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Lorenzo,\n\nThe main purpose is to add permission to transform creation. It is to address the security reviewer\u0027s concerns of not protecting `requrestIpSecTransformState`.\n\nBy requiring permission for creating transform we achieve following things:\n- Added a permission protection to`requrestIpSecTransformState` (since transforms are UID-exclusive object)\n- Created consistent permission models for transport and tunnel mode:\n  - Permission is required for creating a tunnel mode transform and subsequently for all operations on this object. E.g. `requrestIpSecTransformState`\n  \nWe\u0027ve also considered about requiring `ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE` for `requrestIpSecTransformState` but then it would be redundant for tunnel mode transform.\n\nAs for applying transform, I added permission for consistency. If you believe this is unnecessary, I\u0027m happy to remove it.",
